WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.950
Simon's simples at the station is going on a train.

00:08.000 --> 00:11.950
There are policemen at the station.

00:12.000 --> 00:15.950
There are policemen on the trains.

00:16.000 --> 00:19.950
They're all working very hard.

00:20.000 --> 00:24.950
Why are the police here? Simon asks a man.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.950
Look, the man says.

00:29.000 --> 00:32.950
Simon looks at the man's newspaper.

00:33.000 --> 00:36.950
Do you know this man? He reads.

00:37.000 --> 00:43.950
He's a spy. Find him. Stop him. Catch him.

00:44.000 --> 00:47.950
Simon looks at the people in the station.

00:48.000 --> 00:53.950
He can see students in jeans and men in suits.

00:54.000 --> 00:57.950
He can see families and children.

00:58.000 --> 01:01.950
He can't see any spies.

01:02.000 --> 01:08.950
Simon's train goes at 11, and it's 1057 now.

01:09.000 --> 01:11.950
Simon runs to the train.

01:12.000 --> 01:15.950
There's an old woman with an umbrella near Simon.

01:16.000 --> 01:18.950
She's walking very fast.

01:19.000 --> 01:21.950
Simon doesn't see her.

01:22.000 --> 01:23.950
He doesn't see her bag.

01:24.000 --> 01:27.950
The old woman's bag hits Simon's foot.

01:28.000 --> 01:30.950
Simon falls.

01:31.000 --> 01:32.950
His bag opens.

01:33.000 --> 01:36.950
His things fall to the ground.

01:37.000 --> 01:39.950
The old woman's bag is open too.

01:40.000 --> 01:42.950
A letter falls out.

01:43.000 --> 01:46.950
Simon puts his things into his bag.

01:47.000 --> 01:50.950
The old woman's letter is with Simon's things.

01:51.000 --> 01:53.950
Simon doesn't see it.

01:54.000 --> 01:57.950
He puts the old woman's letter in his bag.

01:58.000 --> 02:01.950
He closes his bag and runs to the train.

02:02.000 --> 02:04.950
Simon sits down in the train.

02:05.000 --> 02:08.950
There's a beautiful girl beside him.

02:09.000 --> 02:11.950
Hello, Simon says.

02:12.000 --> 02:14.950
Hello, the girl says.

02:15.000 --> 02:18.950
The old woman's on the train too.

02:19.000 --> 02:22.950
She's looking at Simon's bag.

02:23.000 --> 02:25.950
She wants her letter.

02:26.000 --> 02:28.950
There are policemen on the train.

02:29.000 --> 02:31.950
They can't find the spy.

02:32.000 --> 02:35.950
The old woman sees the policeman.

02:36.000 --> 02:39.950
She turns and walks quickly down the train.

02:40.000 --> 02:42.950
Simon likes the girl.

02:43.000 --> 02:45.950
She likes him.

02:46.000 --> 02:50.950
There's a restaurant on the train. Simon says.

02:51.000 --> 02:53.950
Do you want a cup of coffee?

02:54.000 --> 02:56.950
Yes, please. The girl says.

02:57.000 --> 03:02.950
Okay, wait here. Simon says.

03:03.000 --> 03:06.950
Simon takes his bag and goes to the restaurant.

03:07.000 --> 03:09.950
The old woman's waiting for him.

03:10.000 --> 03:12.950
Simon doesn't see her.

03:13.000 --> 03:15.950
The train's going fast.

03:16.000 --> 03:18.950
Simon falls.

03:19.000 --> 03:21.950
The old woman falls too.

03:22.000 --> 03:24.950
She sits down on the floor.

03:25.000 --> 03:28.950
Oh, I'm sorry, Simon says.

03:29.000 --> 03:31.950
He helps the old woman.

03:32.000 --> 03:35.950
Simon sees the old woman's shoes.

03:36.000 --> 03:40.950
He looks at her shoes and he looks at her face.

03:41.000 --> 03:45.950
They're not women's shoes, Simon thinks.

03:46.000 --> 03:50.950
Simon buys the coffee and goes back to the girl.

03:51.000 --> 03:53.950
The train stops.

03:54.000 --> 03:57.950
Simon and the girl are going on a boat now.

03:58.000 --> 04:01.950
They walk from the train to the boat.

04:02.000 --> 04:04.950
There are policemen here too.

04:05.000 --> 04:08.000
What do they want?

04:09.000 --> 04:10.950
What do they want?

04:11.000 --> 04:12.950
The girl asks.

04:13.000 --> 04:16.950
There's a spy. Simon says.

04:17.000 --> 04:19.950
A spy? The girl says.

04:20.000 --> 04:22.950
I can't see any spies.

04:23.000 --> 04:25.950
Simon looks too.

04:26.000 --> 04:28.950
He sees families and students.

04:29.000 --> 04:30.950
He sees the old woman.

04:31.000 --> 04:34.950
No. Simon says.

04:35.000 --> 04:38.950
I can't see any spies.

04:39.000 --> 04:41.950
It's a beautiful day.

04:42.000 --> 04:45.950
The sun's shining and the water's blue.

04:46.000 --> 04:50.950
Simon and the girl sit near the water and wait.

04:51.000 --> 04:53.950
The boat's coming.

04:54.000 --> 04:57.950
What's your name? Simon asks.

04:58.000 --> 05:00.950
Samantha. The girl says.

05:01.000 --> 05:03.950
Oh, Simon says.

05:04.000 --> 05:05.950
My name's Simon.

05:06.000 --> 05:08.950
Simon and Samantha.

05:09.000 --> 05:11.950
That's nice.

05:12.000 --> 05:14.950
Simon and Samantha are talking.

05:15.000 --> 05:17.950
They don't see the old woman.

05:18.000 --> 05:21.950
They don't see her umbrella.

05:22.000 --> 05:25.950
Look out! A man shouts.

05:26.000 --> 05:27.950
There's a lorry!

05:28.000 --> 05:31.950
Simon and Samantha look.

05:32.000 --> 05:35.950
A lorry is coming down the road very fast.

05:36.000 --> 05:38.000
They jump back.

05:42.000 --> 05:44.950
The old woman jumps back too.

05:45.000 --> 05:48.950
Simon sees the trousers.

05:49.000 --> 05:53.950
They're not women's trousers. Simon thinks.

05:54.000 --> 05:54.950
Come on, Simon.

05:55.000 --> 05:58.950
The boat's here. Samantha says.

05:59.000 --> 06:02.950
Simon and Samantha get on the boat.

06:03.000 --> 06:07.950
Simon opens his bag and takes his lunch out.

06:08.000 --> 06:13.950
He takes the old woman's letter out too, but he doesn't see it.

06:14.000 --> 06:17.950
Do you want a sandwich? Simon asks Samantha.

06:18.000 --> 06:21.950
Yes, please. Samantha says.

06:22.000 --> 06:25.950
She takes her lunch out of her bag.

06:26.000 --> 06:29.950
Do you want an apple? She says.

06:30.000 --> 06:31.950
The old woman's behind them.

06:32.000 --> 06:35.950
Simon and Samantha don't see her.

06:36.000 --> 06:38.950
They don't see her hand.

06:39.000 --> 06:41.950
The boat's going fast now.

06:42.000 --> 06:44.950
The wind's strong.

06:45.000 --> 06:47.950
Samantha's hair goes in her eyes.

06:48.000 --> 06:51.950
The wind takes the old woman's letter.

06:52.000 --> 06:54.950
The letter flies along the boat.

06:55.000 --> 06:58.950
What's that paper? Samantha says.

06:59.000 --> 07:00.950
Is it your boat, ticket?

07:01.000 --> 07:04.950
I don't know. Simon says.

07:05.000 --> 07:06.950
Simon runs.

07:07.000 --> 07:08.950
He wants his ticket.

07:09.000 --> 07:10.950
The old woman runs too.

07:11.000 --> 07:13.950
She wants her letter.

07:14.000 --> 07:16.950
Simon and the old woman run fast.

07:17.000 --> 07:20.000
They're near the paper now.

07:21.000 --> 07:23.950
What's that?

07:24.000 --> 07:25.950
It's a dog.

07:26.000 --> 07:27.950
He's running very fast.

07:28.000 --> 07:32.950
He runs to the paper and catches it in his mouth.

07:33.000 --> 07:36.950
My ticket. Simon says.

07:37.000 --> 07:40.950
My letter. The old woman says.

07:41.000 --> 07:43.950
The dog runs along the boat.

07:44.000 --> 07:47.950
Catch the dog. Simon says.

07:48.000 --> 07:51.950
Stop him! Says the old woman.

07:52.000 --> 07:53.950
The dog's happy.

07:54.000 --> 07:55.950
He can run fast.

07:56.000 --> 07:59.950
He's playing a game with Simon and the old woman.

08:00.000 --> 08:02.950
He doesn't see Samantha.

08:03.000 --> 08:05.950
Samantha jumps up and catches him.

08:06.000 --> 08:09.950
I've got him, Simon. Samantha says.

08:10.000 --> 08:13.950
Simon and the old woman run to Samantha.

08:14.000 --> 08:16.950
The paper's in the dog's mouth.

08:17.000 --> 08:18.950
Simon looks at it.

08:19.000 --> 08:21.950
That's not my ticket. He says.

08:22.000 --> 08:24.950
No. The old woman says.

08:25.000 --> 08:26.950
It's my letter.

08:27.000 --> 08:29.950
The dog likes Simon and Samantha.

08:30.000 --> 08:32.950
But he doesn't like the old woman.

08:33.000 --> 08:36.950
He takes her coat in his mouth and pulls it.

08:37.000 --> 08:39.950
The coat falls to the ground.

08:40.000 --> 08:42.950
The wind takes the old woman's hat.

08:43.000 --> 08:44.950
It falls into the water.

08:45.000 --> 08:47.950
The hair falls with the hat.

08:48.000 --> 08:51.950
Simon and Samantha look at the old woman.

08:52.000 --> 08:53.950
It's not an old woman.

08:54.000 --> 08:55.950
It's a man.

08:56.000 --> 08:59.950
The spy. Simon says.

09:00.000 --> 09:02.950
Police, come here.

09:03.000 --> 09:07.950
The police are very happy.

09:08.000 --> 09:12.950
Thank you, Simon. They say.

09:13.000 --> 09:15.950
Now we have the spy.

09:16.000 --> 09:18.950
But the spy has a letter.

09:19.000 --> 09:22.950
The letter has names and addresses on it.

09:23.000 --> 09:26.950
We want the letter, but we can't find it.

09:27.000 --> 09:28.950
Where is it?

09:29.000 --> 09:30.950
Do you know?

09:31.000 --> 09:33.950
Simon looks at the dog.

09:34.000 --> 09:36.950
The dog looks at Simon.

09:37.000 --> 09:40.950
There's the letter. Simon says.

09:41.000 --> 09:43.950
Where? Says the policeman.

09:44.000 --> 09:49.000
It's in the dog, Simon says.
